# Valgrind suppressions for the typio leak gate (CI job
# `valgrind-leak-gate`). Everything in here is a leak owned by an upstream
# library's process-lifetime pattern, not by typio or optics/flux — the same
# rationale as optics' tools/lsan.supp. A real typio-side leak still fails
# the gate: nothing below matches flux or typio frames.

# fontconfig keeps a per-pattern element array alive for the process
# lifetime (FcPatternObjectInsertElt from config XML parsing). Upstream
# owns it; library teardown cannot release it. Mirrors optics' single
# LSAN suppression `leak:libfontconfig`.
{
   fontconfig-pattern-elt-cache
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite,indirect
   ...
   fun:FcPatternObjectInsertElt
}
{
   fontconfig-pattern-append
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite,indirect
   ...
   fun:FcPatternObjectAddWithBinding*
}
